[26] The Board is presumed to have considered all of the evidence, and is not obliged to refer to every detail of such evidence unless, of course, the contrary is shown.
Florea v. Canada (Minister of Employment and Immigration), [1993] F.C.J. No. 598 (F.C.A.) (QL);
Zhou v. Canada (Minister of Employment and Immigration), [1994] F.C.J. No. 1087 (QL);
